Yet Another Nifty Idea (well, okay, maybe N stands for
nasty here...)

Weilding a cockatrice corpse should result in a smallish
(%10?) chance of your leather gloves turning to stone.
Gauntlets made of metal should be unaffected, but leather
is, at some slight remove, just another kind of "flesh"
and ought to be at least potentially subject to the
flesh-to-stone effect of the cockatrice.

Wearing gloves of stone would be irritating; first of
all you couldn't let go of anything (in this case meaning
you couldn't let go of the cockatrice).

After N turns the cockatrice corpse will rot away anyhow,
so your hands will be empty, but then you couldn't pick
anything up.

Also, you would lose your mastery of doorknobs, latches,
etc, and wouldn't be able to cast most spells.

Remove curse shouldn't touch it; these are not cursed,
they are just transformed into stone.

Appropriate means of breaking your gloves off should be
available;  A friendly creature with a bashing implement
such as a mace or hammer could do it if #chat'ted with
and asked, although this might also damage you. But, you
might not want some particularly nifty gloves destroyed
like that.

Any kind of stone-to-flesh effect should undo it.
#dip'ing your hands in the right potion should also
restore the gloves, but you'll probably have to break
the bottle instead of being able to actually open it.

A character wearing a RoDS or similar under the gloves
should still be able to invoke it.  Wishes to be rid of
the gloves or have them restored should work, as should
wishing for stone-to-flesh.  Any wished-for item or
artifact, should appear in-hand, inside your stony grip.
You wouldn't be able to let go of it then, any more than
you could let go the cockatrice corpse.

Maybe nymphs can figure out a way to steal your stone gloves
without breaking them.  Maybe foocubi can get them off
without breaking them.  (of course, maybe the foocubus is
into bondage and won't bother). Praying at a coaligned
altar should get them removed or restored if Divine
Intervention is successful.

